1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:03,108
[♪ upbeat music plays]

2
00:00:30,427 --> 00:00:34,056
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

3
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION
SOME SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

4
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

5
00:00:49,738 --> 00:00:51,740
[♪ mischievous music plays]

6
00:00:57,496 --> 00:00:59,039
You lying bastard!

7
00:00:59,706 --> 00:01:00,707
[gasps]

8
00:01:04,211 --> 00:01:06,380
What are you gonna do
about my precious money?

9
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:08,632
What are you gonna do about my 15 million?

10
00:01:08,715 --> 00:01:10,592
Oh, no. What do we do?

11
00:01:10,676 --> 00:01:12,302
Oh, no.

12
00:01:13,178 --> 00:01:14,471
Are you okay?

13
00:01:14,554 --> 00:01:16,932
[gasps] Mr. Park! What are you doing?

14
00:01:17,015 --> 00:01:20,977
The insurance company told me
that I have angina,

15
00:01:21,061 --> 00:01:22,354
not myocardial infarction!

16
00:01:23,105 --> 00:01:25,148
And they won't cover angina.

17
00:01:25,232 --> 00:01:29,569
-You did this just because of that?
-"Just because of that"? Wow.

18
00:01:30,362 --> 00:01:32,030
So 15 million is a joke to you?

19
00:01:32,781 --> 00:01:33,990
[sighs]

20
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:37,327
When angina progresses,
it becomes a myocardial infarction.

21
00:01:37,411 --> 00:01:38,537
Exactly!

22
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,580
So it wasn't a myocardial infarction!

23
00:01:41,331 --> 00:01:44,418
You should've just given me
antacids like I said,

24
00:01:44,501 --> 00:01:46,169
so I could've gone
to the hospital next morning!

25
00:01:46,253 --> 00:01:48,755
Why the hell did you cause
such a scene with the chopper?

26
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:51,883
I'm out 15 million
and can't even get my insurance payout.

27
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:55,345
If I had prescribed you antacids
and let you wait to go to the hospital,

28
00:01:56,555 --> 00:01:57,722
you would've gotten it.

29
00:02:00,475 --> 00:02:01,810
As a life insurance payout.

30
00:02:01,893 --> 00:02:03,854
-What are you saying?
-What?

31
00:02:03,937 --> 00:02:05,188
[Hari] No…

32
00:02:05,272 --> 00:02:06,815
Life insurance?

33
00:02:08,275 --> 00:02:09,860
You goddamn quack!

34
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:12,404
Mr. Park! Let's talk it out!

35
00:02:12,487 --> 00:02:14,448
-Let go!
-Let go of…

36
00:02:15,782 --> 00:02:17,075
-You…
-[Hari] Mr. Park.

37
00:02:17,159 --> 00:02:19,703
There seems to be a misunderstanding.

38
00:02:19,786 --> 00:02:21,830
We'll check on the situation first

39
00:02:21,913 --> 00:02:23,331
-and…
-[Jiui screams]

40
00:02:23,415 --> 00:02:25,625
We're really sorry! Just a second!

41
00:02:27,002 --> 00:02:28,044
[Mr. Park] Hey!

42
00:02:28,545 --> 00:02:30,338
Where do you think you're going?

43
00:02:30,422 --> 00:02:32,382
You lying quack!

44
00:02:32,466 --> 00:02:34,593
Give me back my 15 million!

45
00:02:34,676 --> 00:02:36,011
[pants]

46
00:02:43,935 --> 00:02:44,936
[sighs]

47
00:02:53,987 --> 00:02:55,655
[screams]

48
00:02:57,449 --> 00:02:58,700
[spits]

49
00:02:59,618 --> 00:03:02,996
EPISODE 3
GETTING THROUGH ANOTHER DAY

50
00:03:03,079 --> 00:03:06,082
[Ms. Hwang] Oh, my. This is bad.

51
00:03:06,166 --> 00:03:09,294
Mr. Park's normally such a gentleman,

52
00:03:09,377 --> 00:03:13,423
but once you get into a fight with him,
he never lets it go.

53
00:03:13,507 --> 00:03:16,176
He's like a bulldog gnawing on a bone.

54
00:03:16,259 --> 00:03:17,260
[growls]

55
00:03:17,344 --> 00:03:18,678
[Ms. Hwang chuckles]

56
00:03:18,762 --> 00:03:20,263
[clears throat]

57
00:03:20,347 --> 00:03:23,183
Anyway, you're really in for it, Dr. Do.

58
00:03:23,266 --> 00:03:24,643
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT

59
00:03:24,726 --> 00:03:25,727
-Auntie.
-We're here.

60
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:27,062
Goodness.

61
00:03:27,145 --> 00:03:29,606
I'm sorry to tell you this…

62
00:03:29,689 --> 00:03:31,066
-What is it?
-[clears throat]

63
00:03:31,775 --> 00:03:34,027
We're all out of ingredients.

64
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:35,403
-You're…
-What?

65
00:03:35,487 --> 00:03:37,531
You're all out of ingredients?

66
00:03:37,614 --> 00:03:42,160
You told us to come over
for pork cutlets just 20 minutes ago.

67
00:03:42,244 --> 00:03:43,495
Exactly.

68
00:03:43,578 --> 00:03:47,415
I swear everything was fine
20 minutes ago, but…

69
00:03:47,999 --> 00:03:49,543
-[sighs]
-[clears throat]

70
00:03:50,335 --> 00:03:52,629
-Hello, Mr. Park.
-Hello.

71
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,464
[Mr. Park sighs]

72
00:03:54,548 --> 00:03:57,259
That's just how the world works.

73
00:03:57,759 --> 00:03:58,760
Isn't it?
STYLE
::cue()

74
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,181
[sighs]

75
00:04:03,265 --> 00:04:07,936
Just a week ago, I myself would have
never guessed that I'd be down 15 million.

76
00:04:08,019 --> 00:04:09,563
You know?

77
00:04:13,692 --> 00:04:16,111
I think it's because of me,
so I'll eat on my own.

78
00:04:16,194 --> 00:04:17,195
We're good now, right?

79
00:04:17,988 --> 00:04:20,073
-Enjoy your meals.
-[Hari] I'll go with him.

80
00:04:20,865 --> 00:04:22,492
I'll see you later. [chuckles]

81
00:04:22,576 --> 00:04:23,827
[Ms. Hwang] Oh, dear.

82
00:04:26,538 --> 00:04:29,165
GENERAL GOODS FOR SALE

83
00:04:31,251 --> 00:04:32,252
[Hari] Gosh.

84
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:39,134
Why did you come with me?

85
00:04:39,217 --> 00:04:41,219
What if Mr. Park starts gunning for you?

86
00:04:42,512 --> 00:04:44,347
Maybe I'll be the one gunning for him.

87
00:04:46,558 --> 00:04:47,976
[chuckles] Don't worry.

88
00:04:51,354 --> 00:04:52,439
[sighs]

89
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,484
Do you regret it?

90
00:04:58,278 --> 00:05:01,072
Do you wish you'd just
pretended not to notice and let him go?

91
00:05:02,073 --> 00:05:03,074
[clicks tongue]

92
00:05:03,658 --> 00:05:07,203
Whether I regret it or not is irrelevant.

93
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:10,874
Because like him or not,
lacerations are lacerations?

94
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:13,960
[sighs]

95
00:05:14,044 --> 00:05:16,963
I'm sure Mr. Park
just lost his temper momentarily

96
00:05:17,047 --> 00:05:19,257
because of the sudden massive bill.

97
00:05:19,758 --> 00:05:21,593
I'm sure he'll let up soon.

98
00:05:21,676 --> 00:05:24,054
What more could he possibly do?

99
00:05:24,137 --> 00:05:25,263
Hmm? [chuckles]

100
00:05:31,061 --> 00:05:32,437
[yelps]

101
00:05:34,773 --> 00:05:35,857
[Jiui] Turns out

102
00:05:36,775 --> 00:05:38,068
there was more he could do.

103
00:05:38,151 --> 00:05:39,402
Goodness me.

104
00:05:39,486 --> 00:05:42,656
Thank you all
for your hard work in the rain.

105
00:05:42,739 --> 00:05:43,740
You're here?

106
00:05:43,823 --> 00:05:45,325
Please don't mention it.

107
00:05:45,408 --> 00:05:49,913
This is the kind of work
we should be doing for our residents.

108
00:05:49,996 --> 00:05:51,998
[Mr. Park chuckles] Well, lookee here.

109
00:05:52,624 --> 00:05:54,125
Dr. Do Jiui.

110
00:05:54,209 --> 00:05:57,003
You're a proper garbage man.

111
00:05:57,087 --> 00:06:01,174
Sure would've been nice
if you had just done that from the start.

112
00:06:01,257 --> 00:06:02,968
That way I'd still have 15 million.

113
00:06:03,051 --> 00:06:04,219
-[staff chuckle]
-[groans]

114
00:06:04,302 --> 00:06:05,762
[Ms. Hwang] Right.

115
00:06:05,845 --> 00:06:07,514
[♪ tense music plays]

116
00:06:08,098 --> 00:06:09,683
I can't take this anymore.

117
00:06:10,725 --> 00:06:11,726
[groans]

118
00:06:12,852 --> 00:06:13,895
-[groans]
-Are you okay?

119
00:06:13,979 --> 00:06:15,355
What was that for?

120
00:06:15,438 --> 00:06:18,274
-I thought a fight was going to--
-[Mr. Park] What?

121
00:06:18,358 --> 00:06:19,818
Do you have something to say?

122
00:06:19,901 --> 00:06:22,028
It's nothing. You take care now.

123
00:06:22,112 --> 00:06:23,571
Of course, he has nothing to say.

124
00:06:23,655 --> 00:06:25,240
Nothing to say, right?

125
00:06:26,908 --> 00:06:28,785
Just try to bear with it.

126
00:06:28,868 --> 00:06:30,745
I'm sure he's just frustrated.

127
00:06:30,829 --> 00:06:33,873
Why do you keep telling me
to bear with it?

128
00:06:34,624 --> 00:06:36,626
What did I do wrong just now?

129
00:06:37,335 --> 00:06:40,922
This is the least we could do for them.
They're the residents, after all.

130
00:06:41,006 --> 00:06:42,298
No.

131
00:06:42,382 --> 00:06:44,509
I won't stand for this anymore.

132
00:06:44,592 --> 00:06:45,969
I have no reason to!

133
00:06:48,013 --> 00:06:49,014
[sighs]

134
00:06:49,848 --> 00:06:51,015
[stammers, sighs]

135
00:06:52,976 --> 00:06:53,977
[sighs]

136
00:06:55,729 --> 00:06:58,523
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

137
00:06:58,606 --> 00:07:01,609
[coughing]

138
00:07:05,029 --> 00:07:08,658
Goodness. Look how inconvenient
things are for the both of us,

139
00:07:08,742 --> 00:07:11,911
because you'll only prescribe me
three days' worth of medicine.

140
00:07:11,995 --> 00:07:13,538
Your cough isn't getting better.

141
00:07:13,621 --> 00:07:16,082
Maybe because the doctor
is bad at his job.

142
00:07:18,001 --> 00:07:22,255
Do you take any other medication
or have you fallen ill before?

143
00:07:22,338 --> 00:07:23,506
Let's see…

144
00:07:23,590 --> 00:07:24,591
No.

145
00:07:27,552 --> 00:07:30,555
Let me take a look in your mouth.
Would you say "Ah" for me?

146
00:07:34,476 --> 00:07:36,186
I'll also take your temperature.

147
00:07:36,686 --> 00:07:38,354
For the love of…

148
00:07:38,438 --> 00:07:40,815
What's with all the prodding and poking?

149
00:07:41,649 --> 00:07:43,401
Chronic coughs are a bad sign.

150
00:07:43,485 --> 00:07:46,404
It might be good
to go to the mainland and get an X-ray--

151
00:07:46,488 --> 00:07:49,699
Why are you so eager
to send patients off to the mainland?

152
00:07:50,575 --> 00:07:52,452
I'm not a sucker like the chief!

153
00:07:52,535 --> 00:07:55,914
I couldn't afford that
in my wildest dreams,

154
00:07:55,997 --> 00:07:57,373
so just give me my meds now!

155
00:07:57,457 --> 00:08:00,585
I'm not a vending machine
that just dispenses your medicine!

156
00:08:01,419 --> 00:08:02,504
What?
STYLE
::cue()

157
00:08:03,463 --> 00:08:04,506
Go wait outside.

158
00:08:06,174 --> 00:08:07,175
Okay.

159
00:08:11,888 --> 00:08:12,972
Allow me to explain--

160
00:08:15,725 --> 00:08:19,437
Hello, ma'am. What brings you in today?

161
00:08:19,521 --> 00:08:22,732
It's the same problem as always. My knees.

162
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:24,234
Your knees?

163
00:08:24,317 --> 00:08:27,195
That's why I've captured these
and brought them with me.

164
00:08:27,862 --> 00:08:30,865
I heard these are amazing
for aching knees.

165
00:08:30,949 --> 00:08:32,951
Oh, ma'am!

166
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:35,078
What are…

167
00:08:35,161 --> 00:08:36,454
-What are those?
-[chuckles]

168
00:08:36,538 --> 00:08:38,456
What do you think?

169
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:42,168
I brought them for bee sting therapy.
You know how to administer it, right?

170
00:08:42,252 --> 00:08:43,336
[chuckles]

171
00:08:43,419 --> 00:08:44,546
Gosh, ma'am.

172
00:08:44,629 --> 00:08:48,424
You're not meant to administer
bee sting therapy using actual bees.

173
00:08:48,508 --> 00:08:51,594
You're supposed to refine the venom
extracted from a honeybee

174
00:08:51,678 --> 00:08:53,513
and inject it using a needle.

175
00:08:54,055 --> 00:08:55,682
So please put that away.

176
00:08:55,765 --> 00:08:58,935
Well, damn.
That was a total waste of time and effort.

177
00:08:59,018 --> 00:09:01,437
[groans]

178
00:09:01,521 --> 00:09:04,399
Ma'am, you'll have to take this with you.

179
00:09:05,108 --> 00:09:08,111
What use would I have for that?
It's not like I can eat it.

180
00:09:08,194 --> 00:09:10,280
[sighs] But I can't eat it either…

181
00:09:12,031 --> 00:09:13,241
-Ms. Eom?
-Yes?

182
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,952
Go take a seat and wait, please.

183
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:19,581
What is it?

184
00:09:21,332 --> 00:09:22,542
[chuckles]

185
00:09:22,625 --> 00:09:24,502
Would you mind putting this away for me?

186
00:09:24,586 --> 00:09:26,588
You want me to put it away?

187
00:09:26,671 --> 00:09:27,797
Why's that?

188
00:09:27,881 --> 00:09:31,259
You think a country bumpkin like me
can handle bees with my bare hands?

189
00:09:32,302 --> 00:09:35,180
N-Not exactly.

190
00:09:36,806 --> 00:09:37,807
[sighs]

191
00:09:38,725 --> 00:09:42,353
Fine. Your wish is my command,
your highness.

192
00:09:44,147 --> 00:09:45,273
-Ooh…
-[gasps]

193
00:09:45,356 --> 00:09:46,733
Cut it out.

194
00:09:48,776 --> 00:09:51,446
-[exclaims]
-Seriously! I told you to cut it out!

195
00:09:51,529 --> 00:09:53,823
Just get out! What's wrong with you?

196
00:09:53,907 --> 00:09:54,991
-[exclaims]
-[screams]

197
00:09:55,074 --> 00:09:57,619
Come on! [breathes shakily]

198
00:09:59,829 --> 00:10:01,748
-[screams]
-[gasps]

199
00:10:01,831 --> 00:10:03,875
It stings!

200
00:10:14,302 --> 00:10:18,014
[exclaiming, screaming]

201
00:10:19,515 --> 00:10:20,767
It stings!

202
00:10:29,525 --> 00:10:31,236
I'm sorry, Ms. Eom.

203
00:10:34,989 --> 00:10:37,158
[sighs] What's going on?

204
00:10:37,242 --> 00:10:39,244
-[Ms. Hwang] Run!
-[Jucheon] Oh, you see…

205
00:10:39,994 --> 00:10:41,871
What is it?

206
00:10:42,372 --> 00:10:44,749
[Jucheon stammers, yelps]

207
00:10:44,832 --> 00:10:47,460
[screaming]

208
00:10:47,543 --> 00:10:50,046
Run for your lives, everyone!

209
00:10:50,546 --> 00:10:53,383
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

210
00:10:57,804 --> 00:10:59,472
-That stings! Get out!
-The door!

211
00:11:00,723 --> 00:11:01,724
Run!

212
00:11:06,479 --> 00:11:08,147
-Stay away!
-Hurry!

213
00:11:08,231 --> 00:11:10,483
-Hurry!
-Stay still!

214
00:11:10,566 --> 00:11:11,567
-Here!
-Stay still!

215
00:11:12,485 --> 00:11:13,653
Stay still!

216
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:15,154
[groans] That stings!

217
00:11:15,238 --> 00:11:17,282
Why are there bees in the center?

218
00:11:17,365 --> 00:11:19,575
-How on earth did this happen?
-Well…

219
00:11:22,203 --> 00:11:23,288
Hold on a minute.

220
00:11:23,913 --> 00:11:25,707
-What about Dr. Chiyeon?
-What?

221
00:11:26,499 --> 00:11:28,042
-Dr. Chiyeon.
-Huh?

222
00:11:28,584 --> 00:11:29,585
Huh?

223
00:11:29,669 --> 00:11:32,672
[panting]

224
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:35,967
EXAM ROOM 2

225
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:39,053
[♪ heroic music plays]

226
00:11:56,571 --> 00:11:58,031
[exclaims]
STYLE
::cue()

227
00:11:58,990 --> 00:12:00,616
That stings. Come on.

228
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:02,035
Stay still.

229
00:12:02,118 --> 00:12:03,369
Seriously.

230
00:12:03,995 --> 00:12:07,123
Are you kidding me?
Look what they've done to my cute face.

231
00:12:07,832 --> 00:12:09,292
This is ridiculous.

232
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:11,252
We got bees unleashed on us,

233
00:12:11,336 --> 00:12:14,255
but Ms. Sinhye's telling us
to just stay put.

234
00:12:14,339 --> 00:12:15,465
Of course, we should.

235
00:12:16,049 --> 00:12:17,592
We're civil servants.

236
00:12:17,675 --> 00:12:19,594
"Civil servants"?

237
00:12:20,303 --> 00:12:23,056
Well, if we're civil servants,

238
00:12:23,139 --> 00:12:25,600
they should at least
cover our expenses properly.

239
00:12:26,267 --> 00:12:29,228
I've been buying my needles
for the past few months.

240
00:12:29,312 --> 00:12:30,772
Self-funded needles!

241
00:12:31,606 --> 00:12:35,610
I know they don't cost that much,
but it really grinds my gears.

242
00:12:35,693 --> 00:12:37,987
-You shouldn't let that bother you.
-Why not?

243
00:12:38,571 --> 00:12:39,822
Because we're doctors.

244
00:12:40,907 --> 00:12:43,368
We shouldn't let money
get in the way of saving lives,

245
00:12:43,451 --> 00:12:44,452
as doctors.

246
00:12:44,535 --> 00:12:46,996
But still, this is a bit…

247
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,206
[Hyeon] It's unfair.

248
00:12:49,123 --> 00:12:50,875
But we're supposed to suck it up

249
00:12:51,918 --> 00:12:53,002
as soldiers.

250
00:12:53,628 --> 00:12:56,339
-You said we were civil servants.
-We are civil servants.

251
00:12:56,923 --> 00:12:58,341
We're also soldiers

252
00:12:59,592 --> 00:13:00,593
and doctors.

253
00:13:00,676 --> 00:13:01,928
Hmm…

254
00:13:02,011 --> 00:13:04,389
Sounds like a fancy way of saying
we're punching bags

255
00:13:04,472 --> 00:13:06,307
that the whole town can use.

256
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,687
That's why you shouldn't try too hard.

257
00:13:13,648 --> 00:13:15,400
Nothing will come of it.

258
00:13:25,034 --> 00:13:28,079
[door opens, closes]

259
00:13:28,162 --> 00:13:32,792
Did something happen to him
before he came to Pyeondongdo?

260
00:13:33,376 --> 00:13:34,460
Uh…

261
00:13:35,503 --> 00:13:40,299
I heard he was sued by a resident
he treated before he came here.

262
00:13:40,383 --> 00:13:41,592
[♪ sentimental music plays]

263
00:13:41,676 --> 00:13:42,677
Someone sued him?

264
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,680
Two patients with puffer fish poisoning
were brought in,

265
00:13:46,305 --> 00:13:51,144
but while he was treating one,
the other one apparently died of shock.

266
00:13:52,145 --> 00:13:56,399
And the family of the deceased
sued Dr. Hyeon.

267
00:13:56,482 --> 00:13:57,525
What? Are you…

268
00:13:58,568 --> 00:14:00,403
That's ridiculous.

269
00:14:01,112 --> 00:14:03,156
What's even more ridiculous

270
00:14:03,239 --> 00:14:06,701
is that the person who survived
also sued him.

271
00:14:07,285 --> 00:14:08,619
Why?

272
00:14:08,703 --> 00:14:10,830
I guess they chose
to side with their own people

273
00:14:10,913 --> 00:14:12,999
rather than the doctor
who saved their life.

274
00:14:15,334 --> 00:14:17,253
-[sighs]
-Even the person he trusted

275
00:14:17,336 --> 00:14:20,464
to be on his side
told Dr. Hyeon not to fight it.

276
00:14:26,387 --> 00:14:30,057
This is the least we could do for them.
They're the residents, after all.

277
00:14:31,058 --> 00:14:33,561
Is Ms. Hari also on the residents' side?

278
00:14:35,479 --> 00:14:37,231
EXAM ROOM

279
00:14:37,815 --> 00:14:39,567
Hello, sir. What brings you here--

280
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:41,485
[resident] Prescribe this for me.

281
00:14:43,070 --> 00:14:44,822
-What?
-I don't have time.

282
00:14:44,906 --> 00:14:46,908
So just prescribe it for me now.

283
00:14:50,161 --> 00:14:51,704
GOPU SYRUP, PSEUDOPHEDINE…

284
00:14:55,416 --> 00:14:57,543
[Hyeon]
That's why you shouldn't try too hard.

285
00:14:57,627 --> 00:14:59,545
Nothing will come of it.

286
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,051
I'll write you a script.

287
00:15:05,134 --> 00:15:07,178
GOPU SYRUP, PSEUDOPHEDINE

288
00:15:07,261 --> 00:15:10,097
[resident] Then, since you're
writing me a script anyway--

289
00:15:10,181 --> 00:15:12,683
I'll give you a lot.
Will 30 days' worth be enough?

290
00:15:12,767 --> 00:15:15,728
Hot damn. That sounds great.

291
00:15:16,354 --> 00:15:17,688
30-DAY PRESCRIPTION

292
00:15:18,814 --> 00:15:19,815
Please wait outside.

293
00:15:19,899 --> 00:15:20,983
Okay.

294
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:25,988
Wasn't expecting that.

295
00:15:31,327 --> 00:15:33,204
[breathes heavily]

296
00:15:34,288 --> 00:15:36,666
[Jiui] True to the name, Pyeondongdo,

297
00:15:37,375 --> 00:15:40,419
where only one thing matters to them
and that is comfort,

298
00:15:40,503 --> 00:15:43,130
I decided to find comfort for myself.

299
00:15:43,714 --> 00:15:48,594
My insides are in a knot,
and I keep gagging.

300
00:15:48,678 --> 00:15:50,972
So I'm here to pick up
some digestive medicine.

301
00:15:51,055 --> 00:15:53,015
I'll write you your usual prescription.

302
00:15:53,099 --> 00:15:55,017
30-DAY PRESCRIPTION

303
00:15:58,104 --> 00:16:02,650
I need some pain relief patches
and some meds for my arthritis.
STYLE
::cue()

304
00:16:02,733 --> 00:16:04,819
Sure. Pick them up on your way out.

305
00:16:09,198 --> 00:16:12,952
I've got canker sores…

306
00:16:13,035 --> 00:16:15,037
I'll prescribe some Oremedy for you.

307
00:16:16,163 --> 00:16:19,333
Well, I don't care about the ointment.

308
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:23,754
I was just wondering why I keep getting
so many canker sores…

309
00:16:24,422 --> 00:16:27,258
Think it's 'cause my immunity's shot?

310
00:16:27,341 --> 00:16:29,760
Do you think exercise
might make them heal?

311
00:16:29,844 --> 00:16:31,470
Exercise for immunity?

312
00:16:32,388 --> 00:16:33,556
Sure. It's great.

313
00:16:33,639 --> 00:16:34,765
You should exercise.

314
00:16:34,849 --> 00:16:37,435
I'm here to get some painkillers.

315
00:16:37,518 --> 00:16:40,146
Would you like Talenol or Iburonfen?

316
00:16:40,938 --> 00:16:42,982
Just give me whatever.

317
00:16:43,816 --> 00:16:44,942
I'll give you both.

318
00:16:45,985 --> 00:16:47,653
Oh… Okay.

319
00:16:48,154 --> 00:16:51,657
[coughing]

320
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,791
I'll prescribe you 30 days' worth.

321
00:17:01,584 --> 00:17:04,712
DAYS: 30

322
00:17:07,465 --> 00:17:08,716
[sighs]

323
00:17:10,051 --> 00:17:11,594
[Ms. Hwang] You're right.

324
00:17:11,677 --> 00:17:13,054
They're both handsome.

325
00:17:13,137 --> 00:17:14,388
-Yes.
-[Jangsu] Yes.

326
00:17:18,809 --> 00:17:20,728
Here's thirty days' worth of medicine.

327
00:17:20,811 --> 00:17:23,564
Take them in the morning and evening,
30 minutes after a meal.

328
00:17:23,647 --> 00:17:27,735
Well, damn. That's more like it.

329
00:17:28,402 --> 00:17:31,822
So 3 times 1 is 3,
which makes it 11,000 won.

330
00:17:31,906 --> 00:17:34,158
-[chuckles] Right.
-[chuckles] Right.

331
00:17:34,241 --> 00:17:36,744
Only take them twice a day
in the morning and evening!

332
00:17:36,827 --> 00:17:38,287
-[Jangsu] Got it.
-Okay.

333
00:17:38,371 --> 00:17:40,706
-Take care!
-See you next time.

334
00:17:48,297 --> 00:17:49,298
[sighs]

335
00:17:51,467 --> 00:17:52,468
[Hari clears throat]

336
00:17:54,637 --> 00:17:56,180
Dr. Do. [chuckles]

337
00:17:56,263 --> 00:17:57,264
Yes?

338
00:17:57,932 --> 00:18:00,685
What's gotten into you recently?

339
00:18:02,603 --> 00:18:03,771
What do you mean?

340
00:18:03,854 --> 00:18:06,148
You prescribe whatever they ask for,

341
00:18:06,232 --> 00:18:08,401
and you send them away so quickly.

342
00:18:08,484 --> 00:18:11,612
And prescribing a month's worth
of cough medicine like that--

343
00:18:11,696 --> 00:18:14,156
You told me to let them have their way.

344
00:18:14,782 --> 00:18:17,284
-What?
-I was doing what you told me to do.

345
00:18:18,411 --> 00:18:22,623
I know now that getting into fights
will do me no good whatsoever.

346
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:26,252
[stammers] That's not what I--

347
00:18:26,335 --> 00:18:30,297
I just need to stick it out for a year,
then leave, safe and sound.

348
00:18:30,381 --> 00:18:31,841
[scoffs]

349
00:18:31,924 --> 00:18:35,469
Whatever happened to "Like them or not,
lacerations are lacerations?"

350
00:18:36,303 --> 00:18:38,180
I guess I adjusted to life here.

351
00:18:41,225 --> 00:18:42,226
I see.

352
00:18:42,810 --> 00:18:45,438
I get what kind of person you are now.

353
00:18:46,939 --> 00:18:47,940
What?

354
00:18:48,023 --> 00:18:51,068
I almost mistook you for a good doctor.

355
00:18:52,945 --> 00:18:54,280
I'm just a civil servant.

356
00:18:55,156 --> 00:18:57,992
Actually, I'm not even a civil servant.
What even am I?

357
00:18:58,075 --> 00:18:59,076
I'm nothing.

358
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:01,078
That's why no one will protect me!

359
00:19:01,162 --> 00:19:03,205
I'm not done talking! Where are you going?

360
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:07,626
Dr. Do.

361
00:19:08,419 --> 00:19:10,880
You'll have to make rounds
on Madeokdo tomorrow.

362
00:19:12,465 --> 00:19:14,592
-M-Madeokdo?
-Yes.

363
00:19:14,675 --> 00:19:17,386
Don't worry, though.
Ms. Yuk will be accompanying you.

364
00:19:17,470 --> 00:19:18,929
[Hari] Ms. Hwang!

365
00:19:19,555 --> 00:19:22,850
Can I go to Madeokdo
with Dr. Hyeon instead?

366
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:25,811
Me?

367
00:19:26,937 --> 00:19:29,273
Well, this would be
our first Madeokdo visit,

368
00:19:29,356 --> 00:19:31,484
so I figured it'd be awkward
for the patients

369
00:19:31,567 --> 00:19:33,736
if they're unacquainted
with both Dr. Do and me.

370
00:19:33,819 --> 00:19:36,197
Wouldn't Dr. Hyeon be better
since he's been there?

371
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,782
Oh…

372
00:19:37,865 --> 00:19:39,950
But Dr. Hyeon said he doesn't want--

373
00:19:40,034 --> 00:19:41,202
[Hyeon] I'll go.

374
00:19:42,244 --> 00:19:43,621
You're going to go on visits?

375
00:19:43,704 --> 00:19:45,080
Let's leave early tomorrow.

376
00:19:45,164 --> 00:19:46,624
Sure. [chuckles]

377
00:19:50,419 --> 00:19:51,879
I guess that settles that.

378
00:19:52,588 --> 00:19:53,589
[Ms. Hwang exclaims]

379
00:19:53,672 --> 00:19:55,549
You must be so happy, Dr. Do!

380
00:19:55,633 --> 00:19:57,635
-[Ms. Hwang chuckles]
-[Jiui sighs]

381
00:19:58,636 --> 00:20:01,305
What does she want from me?

382
00:20:04,266 --> 00:20:05,267
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

383
00:20:09,647 --> 00:20:11,524
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER
CLOSED

384
00:20:19,615 --> 00:20:20,616
START

385
00:20:20,699 --> 00:20:21,700
RECORD, STOP

386
00:20:23,911 --> 00:20:24,995
[sighs]

387
00:20:25,079 --> 00:20:28,082
[♪ serene music plays]

388
00:20:59,947 --> 00:21:02,825
[pants]

389
00:21:12,543 --> 00:21:13,544
What the…

390
00:21:14,128 --> 00:21:17,631
It's not like I said anything wrong.
Why do I have to bear with everything?

391
00:21:17,715 --> 00:21:18,757
[scoffs]

392
00:21:19,258 --> 00:21:22,469
[phone buzzing]

393
00:21:24,096 --> 00:21:25,097
Hello?

394
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:27,182
Dr. Jiui, where are you?

395
00:21:27,266 --> 00:21:29,768
The supplies we ordered are here.

396
00:21:29,852 --> 00:21:31,520
Could you pick them up for us?

397
00:21:31,604 --> 00:21:32,605
Thanks.

398
00:21:33,397 --> 00:21:34,857
-[line disconnects]
-Hey…

399
00:21:37,818 --> 00:21:39,236
I can't even…

400
00:21:39,945 --> 00:21:41,572
Only take what's yours!

401
00:21:42,239 --> 00:21:44,158
-Okay?
-Okay.

402
00:21:44,241 --> 00:21:46,452
You don't wanna take someone else's stuff.

403
00:21:46,994 --> 00:21:48,537
-This one's mine.
-Yeah.

404
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:54,543
Looking for your delivery?

405
00:21:55,419 --> 00:21:56,420
Yes.

406
00:21:57,046 --> 00:21:58,505
[Mr. Park] Look hard.

407
00:21:59,298 --> 00:22:04,678
I've had hand tremors
ever since I lost 15 million.

408
00:22:04,762 --> 00:22:06,889
I might have dropped it somewhere.

409
00:22:06,972 --> 00:22:09,058
Those were supplies for the health center!

410
00:22:09,141 --> 00:22:11,101
That's none of my concern,

411
00:22:11,185 --> 00:22:13,771
just as my 15 million
was none of your concern.

412
00:22:14,355 --> 00:22:17,483
-[scoffs]
-[groans]

413
00:22:18,442 --> 00:22:19,568
Oh!

414
00:22:19,652 --> 00:22:20,903
There it is.

415
00:22:20,986 --> 00:22:22,821
The delivery for the Public Health Center.

416
00:22:31,163 --> 00:22:36,001
On your way back,
drop off those remaining deliveries. Okay?

417
00:22:37,044 --> 00:22:38,087
What?

418
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:40,089
They're all for old folks here.

419
00:22:40,839 --> 00:22:44,760
Isn't it a PH doc's duty to do everything
for the health of the residents?

420
00:22:46,887 --> 00:22:47,930
Isn't it?

421
00:22:48,013 --> 00:22:50,432
PYEONDONGDO VILLAGE HALL

422
00:22:50,516 --> 00:22:51,892
Use this if you want to.

423
00:22:53,227 --> 00:22:54,561
[scoffs]

424
00:22:55,938 --> 00:22:57,815
Are you sure that's yours?

425
00:23:07,574 --> 00:23:08,575
What are you doing?

426
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:10,369
Ah…

427
00:23:10,452 --> 00:23:13,038
I'm putting on sunscreen.
I don't want to get burned.

428
00:23:13,122 --> 00:23:14,873
The sun's not even up yet though.

429
00:23:14,957 --> 00:23:17,292
Sunscreen's super important, you know.

430
00:23:18,168 --> 00:23:19,503
Oh…

431
00:23:19,586 --> 00:23:20,963
Do you want some?

432
00:23:21,046 --> 00:23:24,049
[♪ comedic music plays]

433
00:23:25,551 --> 00:23:26,552
What is it?

434
00:23:27,886 --> 00:23:29,138
It's nothing.

435
00:23:29,221 --> 00:23:31,724
Come on. Put some on, okay?

436
00:23:31,807 --> 00:23:34,810
You're meant to apply it all the time.

437
00:23:34,893 --> 00:23:38,063
Early in the morning, late at night,
before bed and even during winter.

438
00:23:38,147 --> 00:23:39,690
No, really. I'm good.

439
00:23:39,773 --> 00:23:41,650
Don't play coy with me.

440
00:23:41,734 --> 00:23:43,694
Men wear it too nowadays.

441
00:23:43,777 --> 00:23:44,987
Give me your hand.

442
00:23:45,070 --> 00:23:46,155
Smear it all over.

443
00:23:47,489 --> 00:23:49,158
Don't miss any spots.

444
00:23:53,746 --> 00:23:56,331
No… Wait!

445
00:24:01,754 --> 00:24:03,172
[sighs] Damn it.

446
00:24:09,219 --> 00:24:11,638
[groans] Seriously…

447
00:24:24,109 --> 00:24:25,903
HANDLE WITH CARE

448
00:24:25,986 --> 00:24:26,987
"Handle with care."

449
00:24:28,447 --> 00:24:29,907
"Handle with care."

450
00:24:33,994 --> 00:24:35,579
Yuk Ha…

451
00:24:35,662 --> 00:24:36,789
RECIPIENT: YUK HARI

452
00:24:36,872 --> 00:24:38,332
Ms. Yuk Hari.

453
00:24:38,415 --> 00:24:39,541
HANDLE WITH CARE
STYLE
::cue()

454
00:24:39,625 --> 00:24:40,834
"Handle with care"?

455
00:24:42,002 --> 00:24:46,507
In the spirit of handling it with care,
I should probably let her know.

456
00:24:46,590 --> 00:24:48,509
Yes, definitely.

457
00:24:49,384 --> 00:24:50,427
Let's see…

458
00:24:56,308 --> 00:24:59,978
Ms. Yuk, I came across your delivery
and it seemed important, so…

459
00:25:03,482 --> 00:25:05,818
What the…

460
00:25:06,652 --> 00:25:08,278
[groans] No!

461
00:25:09,321 --> 00:25:10,322
Delete.

462
00:25:11,073 --> 00:25:13,117
Come on. Delete.

463
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,701
THIS MESSAGE HAS BEEN DELETED
FOR YOU ONLY

464
00:25:14,785 --> 00:25:16,203
No! Wait!

465
00:25:17,621 --> 00:25:20,999
[gasps, exclaims]

466
00:25:23,210 --> 00:25:25,462
What… What am I going to do?

467
00:25:26,296 --> 00:25:28,423
[exclaims] Come on!

468
00:25:28,507 --> 00:25:31,635
PYEONDONGDO, MADEOKDO, GAYEONGDO

469
00:25:31,718 --> 00:25:32,719
[phone chimes]

470
00:25:34,388 --> 00:25:35,931
[gasps] What the heck?

471
00:25:36,849 --> 00:25:38,392
-What is this?
-What's wrong?

472
00:25:39,268 --> 00:25:40,519
What?

473
00:25:40,602 --> 00:25:41,854
Uh…

474
00:25:41,937 --> 00:25:43,397
It's nothing.

475
00:25:47,860 --> 00:25:48,861
Oh, my.

476
00:25:48,944 --> 00:25:50,445
Thank you for coming.

477
00:25:50,529 --> 00:25:51,697
I'm the village chief.

478
00:25:51,780 --> 00:25:53,699
[chuckles]

479
00:25:53,782 --> 00:25:55,075
Goodness me.

480
00:25:55,159 --> 00:25:56,660
I guess you had a pretty rough trip.

481
00:25:57,244 --> 00:25:58,495
You're as pale as a ghost.

482
00:25:59,204 --> 00:26:01,957
-Excuse me?
-It's nothing. Come this way.

483
00:26:11,425 --> 00:26:13,343
[Ms. Hwang] You brought the packages?

484
00:26:13,427 --> 00:26:15,512
-Yes.
-[Ms. Hwang] Well done.

485
00:26:15,596 --> 00:26:17,264
Now organize everything in there.

486
00:26:18,140 --> 00:26:19,725
Organize everything too?

487
00:26:28,108 --> 00:26:30,694
RECIPIENT: YUK HARI

488
00:26:37,201 --> 00:26:38,577
What brings you here today?

489
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:43,957
Doctor, my boy, Juman,
normally eats like he's got a hollow leg,

490
00:26:44,041 --> 00:26:46,919
but today he hasn't touched
his food all day.

491
00:26:47,002 --> 00:26:48,962
Not even a drop of water.

492
00:26:50,130 --> 00:26:51,798
He has a hollow leg?

493
00:26:53,133 --> 00:26:56,970
He normally has a large appetite
but didn't even have a sip of water today.

494
00:26:57,054 --> 00:26:58,055
Ah…

495
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:00,265
I'll need to examine the patient.

496
00:27:00,349 --> 00:27:02,851
Is he not able to come here?

497
00:27:02,935 --> 00:27:03,977
Oh, my.

498
00:27:04,061 --> 00:27:05,604
He's here with me.

499
00:27:05,687 --> 00:27:07,564
Goodness, Juman. Get out here.

500
00:27:07,648 --> 00:27:08,982
-Goodness me.
-[Juman whimpers]

501
00:27:10,234 --> 00:27:12,611
Please hurry and take a look at him.

502
00:27:12,694 --> 00:27:15,239
I'm worried my son might be sick!

503
00:27:17,282 --> 00:27:20,661
[Juman whimpers]

504
00:27:20,744 --> 00:27:22,788
Goodness.

505
00:27:22,871 --> 00:27:24,289
You haven't treated him yet.

506
00:27:24,373 --> 00:27:26,375
Where are you going?

507
00:27:26,458 --> 00:27:31,380
MADEOKDO SENIOR CENTER

508
00:27:31,463 --> 00:27:33,882
That old woman, she's not exactly normal.

509
00:27:33,966 --> 00:27:36,385
She's not all there.

510
00:27:36,468 --> 00:27:39,554
She thinks that dog is her son
who died when he was little.

511
00:27:40,138 --> 00:27:42,182
-Ah…
-[sighs]

512
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,351
[village chief] Gosh.

513
00:27:46,770 --> 00:27:47,771
[Hari] But… [sighs]

514
00:27:49,439 --> 00:27:51,566
-Oh, man.
-[sighs]

515
00:27:57,406 --> 00:27:58,573
[line connects]

516
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:02,285
[Hyeon] Bro, can you talk right now?

517
00:28:03,996 --> 00:28:06,873
Well, she's saying that her dog
won't eat or drink any water.

518
00:28:06,957 --> 00:28:08,500
What am I supposed to do?

519
00:28:10,711 --> 00:28:11,837
The weight?

520
00:28:12,879 --> 00:28:14,381
Around three kilos, I think?

521
00:28:16,508 --> 00:28:18,802
Okay, I'll get back to you later.

522
00:28:20,345 --> 00:28:21,763
-Yeah.
-[line disconnects]

523
00:28:22,514 --> 00:28:24,641
[inhales sharply] Juman…

524
00:28:31,773 --> 00:28:33,150
How's Juman doing?

525
00:28:34,860 --> 00:28:37,154
It's not serious, is it?

526
00:28:37,237 --> 00:28:40,240
If Juman ends up passing away,
I'll follow him.

527
00:28:46,621 --> 00:28:49,166
I think we should monitor him
for a couple days.

528
00:28:50,083 --> 00:28:53,795
Could be he's being fussy with food,
so try giving him treats he likes.

529
00:28:53,879 --> 00:28:57,007
If he eats his treats,
he's probably not sick.

530
00:28:57,883 --> 00:29:00,635
Goodness, I don't know how to thank you.

531
00:29:00,719 --> 00:29:04,139
Juman, thank the good doctor, okay?

532
00:29:04,931 --> 00:29:06,516
Okay. Goodbye, Juman.

533
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:07,768
-[barks, growls]
-[Hyeon groans]

534
00:29:07,851 --> 00:29:09,269
Are you okay?

535
00:29:09,352 --> 00:29:10,395
Oh, goodness me.

536
00:29:10,479 --> 00:29:11,813
[groans, sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

537
00:29:16,860 --> 00:29:18,028
[sighs]

538
00:29:18,111 --> 00:29:20,280
I was peeling onions for the dinner shift,

539
00:29:20,363 --> 00:29:22,741
but I ended up peeling my fingers as well.

540
00:29:23,575 --> 00:29:24,868
[Geumja groans]

541
00:29:26,995 --> 00:29:30,540
It's a big wound and it's deep,
so I think you'll need stitches.

542
00:29:30,624 --> 00:29:33,085
You should go to the mainland
to get it treated.

543
00:29:33,168 --> 00:29:34,377
The mainland?

544
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:36,588
What am I going to do?

545
00:29:36,671 --> 00:29:38,882
We even have a group reservation today.

546
00:29:39,591 --> 00:29:42,052
[sighs] Can't I get it treated here?

547
00:29:42,719 --> 00:29:44,429
[Jiui] It's a big wound and it's deep.

548
00:29:46,181 --> 00:29:48,391
If she were to file a complaint
about it leaving a scar…

549
00:29:48,475 --> 00:29:50,560
It's because there might be nerve damage.

550
00:29:52,062 --> 00:29:54,189
You'll want to get a proper checkup.

551
00:29:55,774 --> 00:29:57,025
[sighs]

552
00:29:57,734 --> 00:29:58,777
[Hyeon groans]

553
00:30:02,781 --> 00:30:04,366
I guess you like dogs, huh?

554
00:30:05,909 --> 00:30:06,910
No.

555
00:30:08,286 --> 00:30:10,372
I'm scared of them
because I got bitten once.

556
00:30:10,997 --> 00:30:11,998
Really?

557
00:30:13,166 --> 00:30:14,167
Then why…

558
00:30:15,836 --> 00:30:17,671
Because it seemed to bother you.

559
00:30:20,924 --> 00:30:21,925
Was that not the case?

560
00:30:24,344 --> 00:30:25,345
[chuckles]

561
00:30:26,388 --> 00:30:27,389
It's just…

562
00:30:28,932 --> 00:30:30,934
She reminded me of my grandma,

563
00:30:32,018 --> 00:30:36,731
and I felt bad for her since the dog
was her only source of warmth.

564
00:30:37,524 --> 00:30:38,692
That's it.

565
00:30:44,489 --> 00:30:47,033
I'm sorry you have to leave
before even grabbing a meal.

566
00:30:47,117 --> 00:30:48,451
You even got bitten by a dog.

567
00:30:48,535 --> 00:30:49,661
Uh… [chuckles]

568
00:30:49,744 --> 00:30:50,912
It's fine.

569
00:30:50,996 --> 00:30:52,998
How about you treat us
to a lot of good food

570
00:30:53,081 --> 00:30:54,541
-on our next visit?
-Okay.

571
00:30:54,624 --> 00:30:56,710
[elderly resident] Doctor!

572
00:30:56,793 --> 00:30:58,253
Doctor!

573
00:30:58,336 --> 00:30:59,963
Doctor!

574
00:31:00,046 --> 00:31:02,382
Oh, no.

575
00:31:02,465 --> 00:31:03,800
This is bad.

576
00:31:03,884 --> 00:31:06,386
My boy, Juman…

577
00:31:06,469 --> 00:31:08,638
Enough! They have to get on their boat!

578
00:31:08,722 --> 00:31:11,308
Oh, gosh! He's bleeding!

579
00:31:11,391 --> 00:31:13,602
He's going to die!

580
00:31:13,685 --> 00:31:15,520
-Look…
-Okay, I'll take a look.

581
00:31:18,982 --> 00:31:19,983
Hey,

582
00:31:20,483 --> 00:31:22,360
stay still.

583
00:31:22,444 --> 00:31:24,237
Let me take a look at you.

584
00:31:25,739 --> 00:31:28,283
-[growls]
-What is it?

585
00:31:29,451 --> 00:31:30,994
There's a splinter stuck in him.

586
00:31:31,620 --> 00:31:33,663
We should remove it and stop the bleeding.

587
00:31:36,333 --> 00:31:37,500
But…

588
00:31:38,793 --> 00:31:39,794
But?

589
00:31:41,713 --> 00:31:43,465
I'm not sure I can do it.

590
00:31:44,925 --> 00:31:47,385
[growls, barks]

591
00:31:49,721 --> 00:31:52,140
[♪ tense music plays]

592
00:31:52,224 --> 00:31:53,433
We don't have time.

593
00:31:53,516 --> 00:31:56,770
Just thirty seconds. No more.
Are you sure you can do this?

594
00:31:58,396 --> 00:31:59,773
Let's do this in one go.

595
00:32:01,650 --> 00:32:02,692
One.

596
00:32:03,568 --> 00:32:04,861
Two.

597
00:32:05,445 --> 00:32:06,738
Three. Now!

598
00:32:21,711 --> 00:32:22,879
[groans]

599
00:32:22,963 --> 00:32:24,965
[♪ comical music plays]

600
00:32:37,269 --> 00:32:39,479
-Done. We did it!
-It's done? We did it?

601
00:32:39,562 --> 00:32:42,357
-I got it out! We did it!
-We did it! [exclaims]

602
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:44,776
How's my Juman doing?

603
00:32:44,859 --> 00:32:46,152
We got it out!

604
00:32:46,945 --> 00:32:50,031
-[chuckles] Look!
-[elderly resident] Oh, thank you so much!

605
00:32:50,115 --> 00:32:52,075
-Thank you.
-You got it out. Wow.

606
00:32:52,158 --> 00:32:54,327
-[elderly resident sobs]
-[Hyeon sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

607
00:32:55,870 --> 00:32:58,081
Thank you.

608
00:32:59,708 --> 00:33:01,042
[groans]

609
00:33:02,752 --> 00:33:03,753
[watch beeps]

610
00:33:07,799 --> 00:33:11,594
Hey, when will they be returning anyway?

611
00:33:11,678 --> 00:33:13,013
[Ms. Hwang] Gosh, I know.

612
00:33:13,722 --> 00:33:17,017
The last boat was a while ago,
so I wonder if they got on.

613
00:33:17,934 --> 00:33:19,519
-Goodness.
-[phone ringing]

614
00:33:20,061 --> 00:33:21,062
Oh… [grunts]

615
00:33:26,318 --> 00:33:28,069
Yes, Public Health Center.

616
00:33:28,153 --> 00:33:32,032
-[Hari] Ms. Hwang…
-Hey, is something wrong?

617
00:33:32,115 --> 00:33:34,367
We had to treat
an urgent last-minute patient

618
00:33:34,451 --> 00:33:36,244
and missed the last boat.

619
00:33:36,328 --> 00:33:38,455
[Ms. Hwang] An urgent last-minute patient?

620
00:33:38,538 --> 00:33:41,666
Don't worry. We treated him well.

621
00:33:41,750 --> 00:33:44,753
Then do you have a place to stay?

622
00:33:44,836 --> 00:33:47,797
Yes. One of the residents here
offered a place.

623
00:33:47,881 --> 00:33:50,675
[Ms. Hwang sighs] That's a relief.

624
00:33:50,759 --> 00:33:53,053
In that case, good luck with that.

625
00:33:53,636 --> 00:33:54,637
Mmm…

626
00:33:55,722 --> 00:33:56,806
What is it?

627
00:33:57,474 --> 00:33:59,059
Something urgent came up,

628
00:33:59,142 --> 00:34:01,936
so Ms. Hari and Dr. Chiyeon
missed the last boat.

629
00:34:02,020 --> 00:34:03,938
They'll be back tomorrow.

630
00:34:04,022 --> 00:34:05,190
T-Tomorrow?

631
00:34:05,273 --> 00:34:06,483
Yes.

632
00:34:06,566 --> 00:34:08,318
Wow. No way.

633
00:34:09,027 --> 00:34:11,613
So these things really do
happen in real life, huh?

634
00:34:12,489 --> 00:34:13,907
What do you mean by that?

635
00:34:14,657 --> 00:34:18,036
It's like something out of
a late '80s movie.

636
00:34:18,620 --> 00:34:20,997
-A movie?
-There he goes again, talking nonsense.

637
00:34:21,831 --> 00:34:22,832
[Jucheon] Get this.

638
00:34:22,916 --> 00:34:27,045
A young man and woman go to an island,
and they miss the last boat.

639
00:34:27,754 --> 00:34:29,506
And you know what happens next?

640
00:34:29,589 --> 00:34:31,841
There's only one room available.

641
00:34:32,842 --> 00:34:33,927
Only one room…

642
00:34:35,720 --> 00:34:36,721
available?

643
00:34:36,805 --> 00:34:38,807
[♪ dramatic music playing]

644
00:34:47,690 --> 00:34:49,234
[innkeeper] What to do?

645
00:34:49,317 --> 00:34:51,653
There's only one room left.

646
00:34:51,736 --> 00:34:52,862
Oh, my!

647
00:34:52,946 --> 00:34:55,407
[Jucheon] The sky's grown dark
in an unfamiliar town.

648
00:34:55,490 --> 00:34:58,576
They're saying they only have one room.

649
00:34:59,160 --> 00:35:03,289
Well, I suppose it cannot be helped.

650
00:35:03,373 --> 00:35:06,334
[Jucheon] They only have
each other to rely on…

651
00:35:06,418 --> 00:35:07,460
[Hari sighs]

652
00:35:08,294 --> 00:35:09,671
Mmm.

653
00:35:10,630 --> 00:35:12,716
-[Hari sighs, gasps]
-Ms. Yuk!

654
00:35:14,384 --> 00:35:16,261
We have plenty of time to spare.

655
00:35:17,053 --> 00:35:18,138
Would you like a drink?

656
00:35:18,221 --> 00:35:19,556
[gasps]

657
00:35:19,639 --> 00:35:22,350
[Jucheon] Since things are awkward,

658
00:35:22,434 --> 00:35:25,311
they naturally gravitate towards
sharing a drink together.

659
00:35:27,397 --> 00:35:29,524
[loudly gulping]

660
00:35:31,568 --> 00:35:33,486
[both sigh]

661
00:35:34,821 --> 00:35:36,197
[Jucheon] One glass

662
00:35:36,281 --> 00:35:37,574
-turns into two…
-[Hari] Cheers.

663
00:35:38,199 --> 00:35:40,160
[Jucheon]
Their glasses keep touching until…

664
00:35:41,035 --> 00:35:44,998
Dr. Chiyeon, I seem to be getting drunk.

665
00:35:46,458 --> 00:35:47,542
Gosh.

666
00:35:47,625 --> 00:35:53,256
I'm already drunk on your scent, Ms. Hari.

667
00:35:53,339 --> 00:35:56,843
[Jucheon] Something else starts touching!

668
00:35:57,510 --> 00:35:58,762
[Jeongseon] Something else?

669
00:35:59,554 --> 00:36:00,889
[Hari gasps]

670
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:05,977
-[Hyeon hums]
-[Hari sighs]

671
00:36:10,064 --> 00:36:12,025
Stop!

672
00:36:12,692 --> 00:36:13,985
[Jucheon] What do you think?

673
00:36:14,068 --> 00:36:15,153
Not bad, huh?

674
00:36:16,196 --> 00:36:18,323
I'm gonna go to my room now.

675
00:36:18,406 --> 00:36:19,741
[Jeongseon] Okay.

676
00:36:19,824 --> 00:36:22,368
[Jucheon] You're going?
Things were just getting spicy.

677
00:36:22,452 --> 00:36:26,831
[Ms. Hwang] Dr. Yong, you really put
too much thought into saying

678
00:36:26,915 --> 00:36:29,626
a whole lot you really don't need to say.

679
00:36:29,709 --> 00:36:30,835
[Jiui] My point exactly!

680
00:36:30,919 --> 00:36:33,421
[Jucheon] I thought
it was super fun, though.
STYLE
::cue()

681
00:36:42,138 --> 00:36:44,349
[innkeeper] What to do?

682
00:36:44,432 --> 00:36:46,643
I'm sorry, but we only have one room left.

683
00:36:47,268 --> 00:36:48,394
Uh…

684
00:36:50,730 --> 00:36:52,732
In that case…

685
00:36:52,816 --> 00:36:55,819
If it's all right with you,
would you like to stay in my room?

686
00:36:55,902 --> 00:36:57,779
Oh, no. That's fine.

687
00:36:57,862 --> 00:37:00,406
We're just grateful
that you're looking out for us.

688
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:04,327
That there's my room,
so tell me if you need anything.

689
00:37:04,410 --> 00:37:05,411
-Okay.
-Okay.

690
00:37:17,632 --> 00:37:19,342
We have plenty of time to spare.

691
00:37:20,426 --> 00:37:21,427
Would you like a drink?

692
00:37:28,810 --> 00:37:31,104
[boat engine running]

693
00:37:35,984 --> 00:37:38,403
They go around just fine,
even late at night.

694
00:37:44,284 --> 00:37:45,702
[Hari] Cheers.

695
00:37:50,498 --> 00:37:52,667
-[Hyeon sighs]
-Wow!

696
00:37:55,545 --> 00:37:58,256
Do you still not remember
the day we first met?

697
00:37:58,339 --> 00:37:59,799
[Hari groans]

698
00:38:00,425 --> 00:38:01,426
Sorry.

699
00:38:03,011 --> 00:38:04,929
Well, that's disappointing.

700
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:08,182
It was the first time in my life
I've ever been rejected.

701
00:38:09,434 --> 00:38:10,643
What?

702
00:38:10,727 --> 00:38:11,978
You rejected me,

703
00:38:12,812 --> 00:38:14,355
when I didn't even ask you out.

704
00:38:15,732 --> 00:38:17,650
-What do you mean by…
-[motorcycle approaching]

705
00:38:17,734 --> 00:38:19,652
[motorcycle crashes]

706
00:38:19,736 --> 00:38:20,904
[body thuds]

707
00:38:23,197 --> 00:38:24,282
[bystander] Hello? Emergency line?

708
00:38:24,365 --> 00:38:27,076
I'm the one who just called
about the motorcycle accident.

709
00:38:27,160 --> 00:38:29,287
Check where they are!

710
00:38:29,370 --> 00:38:30,914
[bystander] Can you tell me where you are?

711
00:38:30,997 --> 00:38:32,624
Yes. She's administering CPR.

712
00:38:32,707 --> 00:38:35,126
I'm an intern at Yeonhui University.
I'll take over.

713
00:38:35,209 --> 00:38:36,878
-Okay.
-[bystander] They're almost here!

714
00:38:37,795 --> 00:38:39,213
[Hari] EMS is on the way.

715
00:38:47,639 --> 00:38:49,140
The patient's breathing again.

716
00:38:51,100 --> 00:38:53,102
EMERGENCY MEDICAL SERVICE TEAM

717
00:39:00,109 --> 00:39:01,152
Good job.

718
00:39:02,820 --> 00:39:03,821
You too.

719
00:39:09,118 --> 00:39:10,203
Wait.

720
00:39:20,505 --> 00:39:21,631
I'm sorry.

721
00:39:22,131 --> 00:39:24,133
-What?
-I have a boyfriend.

722
00:39:25,301 --> 00:39:28,054
-Hey, wait--
-I told you I have a boyfriend.

723
00:39:29,347 --> 00:39:30,515
That's great.

724
00:39:30,598 --> 00:39:33,059
I'm sure your boyfriend
will want to reach you,

725
00:39:33,142 --> 00:39:34,602
-so take this with you.
-What?

726
00:39:38,940 --> 00:39:40,316
This is yours.

727
00:39:44,487 --> 00:39:45,822
Oh, my.

728
00:39:45,905 --> 00:39:47,615
I see. How did it…

729
00:39:47,699 --> 00:39:51,077
You don't seem like
love-at-first-sight material.

730
00:39:51,828 --> 00:39:53,121
What?

731
00:39:53,204 --> 00:39:55,289
Look in the mirror.
You'll see what I mean.

732
00:39:55,373 --> 00:39:56,499
Move aside.

733
00:40:01,379 --> 00:40:02,588
What's wrong with my face?

734
00:40:10,179 --> 00:40:11,180
[chuckles]

735
00:40:12,223 --> 00:40:13,391
[chuckles]

736
00:40:14,726 --> 00:40:15,935
[Hari gasps]

737
00:40:16,019 --> 00:40:17,270
You're the guy from…

738
00:40:17,353 --> 00:40:19,063
-[chuckles]
-[Hari gasps loudly]

739
00:40:19,147 --> 00:40:20,356
Right?

740
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:22,734
Wow. [laughs]

741
00:40:23,651 --> 00:40:26,696
I'm really not usually like that.

742
00:40:26,779 --> 00:40:29,866
I was just so out of it and that was just…

743
00:40:29,949 --> 00:40:32,577
-Pretty sure you're still the same.
-I'm not!

744
00:40:33,411 --> 00:40:34,537
[Hyeon chuckles]

745
00:40:42,503 --> 00:40:44,422
It's meant to be handled with care.

746
00:40:45,089 --> 00:40:47,008
It should be handled with care.

747
00:40:48,801 --> 00:40:50,720
And we wouldn't want
anyone stealing it, so…

748
00:40:55,391 --> 00:40:56,809
I'll just put it over there.

749
00:40:56,893 --> 00:40:59,812
[Mija] Hi, Hari.
How are things over there?

750
00:40:59,896 --> 00:41:01,814
Do you have a place to stay?

751
00:41:01,898 --> 00:41:04,525
Goodness. Don't worry about me.

752
00:41:04,609 --> 00:41:06,652
I'll take care of myself.
STYLE
::cue()

753
00:41:06,736 --> 00:41:09,822
Okay, I'm hanging up now.

754
00:41:12,784 --> 00:41:13,868
[grunts]

755
00:41:14,660 --> 00:41:16,746
-[Mija] Burglar!
-Wait!

756
00:41:16,829 --> 00:41:19,082
[Jiui yelling]

757
00:41:19,165 --> 00:41:21,876
Who are you?

758
00:41:21,959 --> 00:41:24,670
Wait! It's me.

759
00:41:28,508 --> 00:41:30,134
[Mija] Oh, my.

760
00:41:30,218 --> 00:41:32,970
-You're the doctor.
-Yes.

761
00:41:33,054 --> 00:41:35,014
What brings you here?

762
00:41:36,265 --> 00:41:38,518
This. A delivery.

763
00:41:40,103 --> 00:41:41,187
Delivery…

764
00:41:41,979 --> 00:41:43,481
Oh, goodness.

765
00:41:44,482 --> 00:41:45,817
I'm sorry, ma'am.

766
00:41:48,528 --> 00:41:50,738
[Mija] Come in.

767
00:41:52,782 --> 00:41:55,451
Sit here for a bit.

768
00:41:55,535 --> 00:41:57,036
I'll bring the medicine.

769
00:42:11,676 --> 00:42:12,677
Here.

770
00:42:13,344 --> 00:42:14,345
Goodness.

771
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,764
Let me see.

772
00:42:26,649 --> 00:42:28,484
Goodness. That's got to hurt.

773
00:42:29,819 --> 00:42:31,112
[Jiui groans]

774
00:42:31,988 --> 00:42:33,072
[Mija laughs]

775
00:42:44,750 --> 00:42:47,170
ONE PAINKILLER
WHEN PAIN BECOMES UNBEARABLE

776
00:42:47,253 --> 00:42:49,213
TALENOL
DON'T TAKE MORE THAN FIVE

777
00:42:50,464 --> 00:42:54,802
But what kind of pain
is making you take so many…

778
00:42:57,096 --> 00:42:59,473
I didn't even get to ask you back then.

779
00:43:00,099 --> 00:43:01,392
[Mija] Well…

780
00:43:01,475 --> 00:43:04,228
It's nothing.

781
00:43:04,312 --> 00:43:05,938
It's just migraines.

782
00:43:07,023 --> 00:43:09,025
It seems to be causing a lot of distress,

783
00:43:09,108 --> 00:43:12,361
but you shouldn't just take painkillers
because you're in pain.

784
00:43:12,445 --> 00:43:14,322
Don't you worry now.

785
00:43:14,405 --> 00:43:15,781
I know my body--

786
00:43:15,865 --> 00:43:17,116
Better than anyone else.

787
00:43:19,535 --> 00:43:23,581
But even if you may think
you know your body best,

788
00:43:23,664 --> 00:43:25,082
you could be wrong.

789
00:43:26,042 --> 00:43:27,877
[♪ sincere music playing]

790
00:43:29,295 --> 00:43:31,047
Unlock your phone for me, please.

791
00:43:31,589 --> 00:43:32,798
What for?

792
00:43:40,473 --> 00:43:45,353
PH DOC DO JIUI

793
00:43:45,436 --> 00:43:46,520
SAVE

794
00:43:47,730 --> 00:43:49,273
This is my number.

795
00:43:49,357 --> 00:43:52,652
Give me a call
if you can't make it over to the center.

796
00:43:52,735 --> 00:43:53,986
Goodness me.

797
00:43:55,071 --> 00:43:56,405
Thank you.

798
00:43:58,866 --> 00:44:00,201
[Hari] I'll sleep on this side.

799
00:44:00,284 --> 00:44:01,911
You sleep on that side.

800
00:44:02,536 --> 00:44:04,664
Are we really going to sleep
in the same room?

801
00:44:04,747 --> 00:44:06,457
Yeah, it's fine.

802
00:44:06,540 --> 00:44:09,835
There are bugs outside.
How can I ask you to sleep outside?

803
00:44:09,919 --> 00:44:11,754
Let's just make do.

804
00:44:11,837 --> 00:44:14,131
I didn't say
I'd be the one sleeping outside.

805
00:44:17,093 --> 00:44:18,094
What?

806
00:44:21,055 --> 00:44:22,265
I mean…

807
00:44:22,348 --> 00:44:23,683
[laughs]

808
00:44:31,732 --> 00:44:33,150
[Hari] What is that?

809
00:44:35,653 --> 00:44:37,738
Did you draw a line in case I cross it?

810
00:44:39,657 --> 00:44:42,827
Wow. What do you take me for?

811
00:44:43,536 --> 00:44:45,246
I should ask the same of you, okay?

812
00:44:46,289 --> 00:44:48,708
Don't you dare.
I'm going to be really mad if you do.

813
00:44:58,134 --> 00:44:59,385
[chuckles]

814
00:45:05,474 --> 00:45:07,476
[♪ amusing music playing]

815
00:45:21,198 --> 00:45:22,616
[sighs]

816
00:45:25,161 --> 00:45:26,370
[Hari snores]

817
00:45:27,663 --> 00:45:29,415
-[Hyoen chuckles]
-[snoring continues]
STYLE
::cue()

818
00:45:38,466 --> 00:45:42,636
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

819
00:45:47,016 --> 00:45:48,476
Good morning, everyone.

820
00:45:48,559 --> 00:45:49,977
Good morning.

821
00:45:51,312 --> 00:45:52,688
Are they back yet?

822
00:45:53,272 --> 00:45:56,442
Dr. Chiyeon's back.
I guess you didn't run into him.

823
00:45:56,525 --> 00:45:57,526
No, I didn't.

824
00:46:00,321 --> 00:46:02,239
What about Ms. Hari?

825
00:46:02,323 --> 00:46:05,409
She took the day off for something.
Do you need something from her?

826
00:46:05,493 --> 00:46:07,495
No, it's nothing.

827
00:46:08,079 --> 00:46:09,413
[phone ringing]

828
00:46:12,958 --> 00:46:15,753
This is PH doc Do Jiui
at the Public Health Center.

829
00:46:15,836 --> 00:46:18,047
Hey, I'm Ko Changmok.

830
00:46:18,130 --> 00:46:19,507
Excuse me?

831
00:46:19,590 --> 00:46:21,342
I said I'm Ko Changmok.

832
00:46:21,425 --> 00:46:24,595
Are you having any issues there?

833
00:46:24,678 --> 00:46:25,679
Sorry?

834
00:46:25,763 --> 00:46:30,309
I'm just calling to see
if you're having any issues over there.

835
00:46:30,393 --> 00:46:31,394
Who's calling?

836
00:46:31,977 --> 00:46:33,979
Someone's asking if we have any issues.

837
00:46:34,063 --> 00:46:37,274
I'm up to my neck in work!
I don't have time to deal with that crap!

838
00:46:37,358 --> 00:46:39,068
Tell them to stop fooling around!

839
00:46:39,151 --> 00:46:41,529
I'm just asking if you have any issues.

840
00:46:41,612 --> 00:46:44,907
We're a little busy right now,
so would you mind visiting the center?

841
00:46:44,990 --> 00:46:47,034
-Hello? He--
-Thank you.

842
00:46:54,125 --> 00:46:56,627
[laughs]

843
00:46:56,710 --> 00:46:58,712
Goodness me,

844
00:46:58,796 --> 00:47:03,509
our Public Health Center
seems to be busy as hell.

845
00:47:03,592 --> 00:47:06,137
This is how things are between me
and our subordinates.

846
00:47:06,220 --> 00:47:10,099
We've done away with all formalities.
We're comfortable with each other.

847
00:47:10,182 --> 00:47:11,183
YEOPOONG-GUN

848
00:47:11,267 --> 00:47:12,893
[laughs]

849
00:47:15,438 --> 00:47:19,150
[narrator] A helicopter cuts its way
across high waves and islands.

850
00:47:19,817 --> 00:47:24,447
Wherever the patients may be,
a helicopter is dispatched, on the double.

851
00:47:25,030 --> 00:47:27,700
A mere 10 minutes
after a patient is reported,

852
00:47:27,783 --> 00:47:30,911
the helicopter
begins transporting the patient

853
00:47:30,995 --> 00:47:33,539
in a stunning display

854
00:47:33,622 --> 00:47:38,502
of Governor Ko Changmok's
health care modernization initiative.

855
00:47:38,586 --> 00:47:40,754
[chuckling]

856
00:47:41,839 --> 00:47:43,966
Now, as much as it pains me
to remember it,

857
00:47:44,049 --> 00:47:46,677
the image of my grandmother
grabbing my wrist

858
00:47:46,760 --> 00:47:49,805
and telling me that
one had no choice but to die

859
00:47:49,889 --> 00:47:52,975
if one were to fall sick on an island
is still seared into my heart.

860
00:47:53,058 --> 00:47:57,605
I promised to modernize health care
in Yeopoong-gun during my term of office,

861
00:47:57,688 --> 00:48:01,066
so I, Ko Changmok,
will do whatever it takes

862
00:48:01,150 --> 00:48:04,820
to overhaul our helipads

863
00:48:04,904 --> 00:48:07,364
so my grandmother's words

864
00:48:07,448 --> 00:48:11,327
don't apply to Yeopoong-gun, everyone!

865
00:48:14,830 --> 00:48:16,415
-Hey, Mr. Choi.
-Yes, sir.

866
00:48:16,499 --> 00:48:18,375
That place we called just now.

867
00:48:18,459 --> 00:48:21,879
Are you sure they recently used
a chopper to transport a patient?

868
00:48:21,962 --> 00:48:22,963
I'm sure of it, sir.

869
00:48:23,047 --> 00:48:25,758
Well, then that's no way
to respond to a call.

870
00:48:25,841 --> 00:48:27,218
I mean, Director,

871
00:48:27,301 --> 00:48:29,678
you said you strengthened
the emergency protocols.

872
00:48:29,762 --> 00:48:32,348
-Did you not finish what you started?
-I'm sorry, sir.

873
00:48:32,431 --> 00:48:33,849
Sorry just won't cut it, okay?

874
00:48:33,933 --> 00:48:37,353
Be sure to punish them
to uphold discipline.

875
00:48:37,436 --> 00:48:39,355
Yes, sir. I'll have a word with them.

876
00:48:39,438 --> 00:48:42,900
Just to be clear,
I told you to punish them.

877
00:48:49,323 --> 00:48:50,491
[sighs]

878
00:49:04,421 --> 00:49:06,048
Perhaps you've fallen ill.

879
00:49:06,590 --> 00:49:08,259
[patient] Of course I've fallen ill.

880
00:49:08,342 --> 00:49:11,637
I'm coughing nonstop, like I told you.

881
00:49:11,720 --> 00:49:14,765
Not even the medicine
my daughter-in-law got me is working.

882
00:49:14,848 --> 00:49:17,601
-Right.
-[patient coughing]

883
00:49:17,685 --> 00:49:22,731
I'm going to have to switch
to a stronger medicine.
STYLE
::cue()

884
00:49:22,815 --> 00:49:25,442
No matter how much I take my current ones,

885
00:49:25,526 --> 00:49:27,444
it doesn't seem to make a difference.

886
00:49:27,528 --> 00:49:29,863
As I said before,
there's a variety of things

887
00:49:29,947 --> 00:49:32,533
-that could be causing your cough…
-For crying out loud.

888
00:49:32,616 --> 00:49:35,119
I told you I know all about that. [coughs]

889
00:49:35,202 --> 00:49:39,873
Just get off my case
and give me stronger cough medicine.

890
00:49:39,957 --> 00:49:41,584
[coughing]

891
00:49:42,835 --> 00:49:46,297
I'll be taking that as a yes
and leaving now.

892
00:49:46,380 --> 00:49:49,300
[continues coughing]

893
00:49:54,430 --> 00:49:56,890
REVOPANSA PILL
DAYS: 30

894
00:49:56,974 --> 00:49:59,018
Morning and evening,
30 minutes after meals.

895
00:49:59,101 --> 00:50:00,853
-You know the drill, right?
-Yes.

896
00:50:01,854 --> 00:50:04,106
I switched to a stronger medicine.

897
00:50:09,153 --> 00:50:10,613
Ms. Hwang.

898
00:50:10,696 --> 00:50:12,906
I'm sorry,
I received the ID photo too late.

899
00:50:12,990 --> 00:50:14,950
You certainly took your sweet time.

900
00:50:15,034 --> 00:50:17,494
I see Mr. Jangsu's switching his meds.

901
00:50:17,578 --> 00:50:20,706
-He said he needed something stronger.
-Is he a doctor or something?

902
00:50:20,789 --> 00:50:22,833
Who's he to tell us
to give him stronger meds?

903
00:50:22,916 --> 00:50:25,127
[sighs] That's how it is
with everyone here.

904
00:50:25,210 --> 00:50:26,795
They all know their own body best.

905
00:50:26,879 --> 00:50:28,589
If he knew his body so well,

906
00:50:28,672 --> 00:50:31,759
how did he end up getting a heart attack
and needing a stent?

907
00:50:31,842 --> 00:50:33,177
What a load of rubbish.

908
00:50:33,719 --> 00:50:34,928
A heart…

909
00:50:36,055 --> 00:50:37,306
Heart attack?

910
00:50:37,973 --> 00:50:39,224
[Ms. Hwang] Didn't he tell you?

911
00:50:39,308 --> 00:50:43,103
Mr. Jangsu also got a stent inserted
last year, just like Mr. Park.

912
00:50:43,187 --> 00:50:45,648
I never heard anything of the sort.

913
00:50:45,731 --> 00:50:47,399
That wasn't in his medical records.

914
00:50:47,483 --> 00:50:48,567
Scoot over.

915
00:50:48,651 --> 00:50:50,903
"Stent insertion, myocardial infarction."

916
00:50:51,737 --> 00:50:53,280
MEDICAL RECORD NOT FOUND

917
00:50:53,364 --> 00:50:55,783
It's not here!

918
00:50:55,866 --> 00:50:58,452
-I guess it hasn't been updated yet.
-[Jiui] Oh, no!

919
00:50:58,535 --> 00:51:02,331
Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs
can cause side effects or death

920
00:51:02,414 --> 00:51:05,084
for patients with a history
of myocardial infarction.

921
00:51:05,167 --> 00:51:07,336
Is he seriously trying to ruin my life?

922
00:51:07,419 --> 00:51:12,800
[on radio] Jangsu's Herbal Medicine.
Let it energize…

923
00:51:12,883 --> 00:51:14,093
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

924
00:51:14,176 --> 00:51:15,803
Are you kidding me right now?

925
00:51:15,886 --> 00:51:20,641
[on radio] Black garlic extract
that's damn good for chronic fatigue,

926
00:51:20,724 --> 00:51:24,812
also great for hangovers,
detoxing your liver, and…

927
00:51:24,895 --> 00:51:26,980
Hey, Mr. Lee Jangsu!

928
00:51:27,856 --> 00:51:28,857
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

929
00:51:29,650 --> 00:51:32,778
[♪ upbeat music playing on speakers]

930
00:51:32,861 --> 00:51:34,071
Hey…

931
00:51:34,154 --> 00:51:35,948
Hey, Mr. Lee Jangsu!

932
00:51:37,991 --> 00:51:39,410
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

933
00:51:39,493 --> 00:51:41,120
♪ Twirl round and round ♪

934
00:51:41,203 --> 00:51:42,204
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

935
00:51:42,287 --> 00:51:43,789
♪ Till the night is over ♪

936
00:51:43,872 --> 00:51:45,541
♪ Twirl round and round ♪

937
00:51:45,624 --> 00:51:46,834
-Mr. Lee!
-♪ Through the night ♪

938
00:51:46,917 --> 00:51:49,586
♪ And until the day goes by ♪

939
00:51:49,670 --> 00:51:51,338
Hey, Lee Jangsu!

940
00:51:53,632 --> 00:51:55,467
Hey, Lee Jangsu!

941
00:51:55,551 --> 00:51:56,552
Goddamn it!

942
00:51:58,637 --> 00:51:59,888
Mr. Lee Jangsu!

943
00:52:03,934 --> 00:52:04,935
I'm back!

944
00:52:07,688 --> 00:52:08,939
Damn.

945
00:52:09,022 --> 00:52:11,859
JANGSU'S HERBAL MEDICINE

946
00:52:11,942 --> 00:52:13,777
You're back?

947
00:52:20,617 --> 00:52:21,618
Seriously.

948
00:52:24,455 --> 00:52:25,622
Lee Jangsu!

949
00:52:30,753 --> 00:52:33,005
What the… Dr. Do?

950
00:52:36,842 --> 00:52:40,304
Mr. Lee, did you have
a heart attack before?

951
00:52:41,472 --> 00:52:42,723
Yes. So what?

952
00:52:42,806 --> 00:52:44,391
Why didn't you tell me that?

953
00:52:45,517 --> 00:52:48,395
I mean, it's not like telling you
would have done any good.

954
00:52:48,479 --> 00:52:50,606
It's not like
you're going to cure my heart!

955
00:52:50,689 --> 00:52:54,443
For someone with a history
of myocardial infarction, NSAIDs…

956
00:52:54,526 --> 00:52:56,320
[Jiui breathes shakily]

957
00:52:58,155 --> 00:52:59,156
The thing is…

958
00:52:59,239 --> 00:53:01,742
you could suffer side effects
if you take those drugs.

959
00:53:01,825 --> 00:53:04,787
It could even kill you,
so give me the meds right now!
STYLE
::cue()

960
00:53:07,623 --> 00:53:10,292
The meds you're taking right now.
Hand those over as well.

961
00:53:10,375 --> 00:53:13,086
The ones my daughter-in-law got for me?

962
00:53:13,170 --> 00:53:15,047
Yes, I need to know what they are.

963
00:53:15,130 --> 00:53:18,300
I'll go get them. Give me a second.

964
00:53:18,383 --> 00:53:20,636
And I prescribed all this
without knowing that!

965
00:53:23,263 --> 00:53:25,516
[panting]

966
00:53:27,893 --> 00:53:30,103
MAPRYL

967
00:53:31,271 --> 00:53:33,190
An ACE inhibitor.

968
00:53:33,732 --> 00:53:36,944
Just as I thought, the coughs
were a side effect of his meds.

969
00:53:38,070 --> 00:53:40,239
The reason you've been coughing,

970
00:53:40,322 --> 00:53:42,991
it's probably a side effect of these meds.

971
00:53:43,075 --> 00:53:44,493
You have to switch right now.

972
00:53:44,576 --> 00:53:47,371
Get a new prescription
from the hospital that did your stent.

973
00:53:47,454 --> 00:53:48,580
Okay.

974
00:53:59,258 --> 00:54:00,384
This is why…

975
00:54:04,429 --> 00:54:09,810
This is why patients have to be
forthcoming about their medical history.

976
00:54:09,893 --> 00:54:13,939
Even if you think you know your body well,
you need to consult your doctor first.

977
00:54:14,022 --> 00:54:15,983
That's what doctors are for!
Do you understand?

978
00:54:18,277 --> 00:54:19,695
I understand.

979
00:54:21,822 --> 00:54:22,823
I'm going now.

980
00:54:27,202 --> 00:54:28,495
Hey, Doctor!

981
00:54:30,497 --> 00:54:31,582
What is it now?

982
00:54:35,252 --> 00:54:37,045
Thank you.

983
00:54:37,129 --> 00:54:39,798
Goodness me. Thank you.

984
00:54:41,508 --> 00:54:47,514
I mean, you came running all this way
just to save my life, didn't you?

985
00:54:47,598 --> 00:54:50,017
Not even my son or my daughter-in-law

986
00:54:50,100 --> 00:54:52,060
would have gone to such lengths
to help me.

987
00:54:52,853 --> 00:54:54,646
[wife] You're absolutely right.

988
00:54:54,730 --> 00:54:56,982
Thank you so much.

989
00:54:57,065 --> 00:55:02,446
I won't touch those pills
for the rest of my life,

990
00:55:02,529 --> 00:55:05,490
-so don't worry about me, okay?
-Right.

991
00:55:10,662 --> 00:55:11,663
Okay.

992
00:55:17,961 --> 00:55:18,962
[wife] Take care.

993
00:55:20,922 --> 00:55:21,923
Goodness.

994
00:55:23,592 --> 00:55:25,886
[Jangsu] Maybe I should've
given him some melons.

995
00:55:25,969 --> 00:55:27,554
[wife] Gosh, you're right.

996
00:55:48,533 --> 00:55:49,743
Hey, Doctor.

997
00:55:50,994 --> 00:55:52,204
Hello there.

998
00:55:53,163 --> 00:55:58,168
I did exactly what you told me to
and did some exercise,

999
00:55:58,251 --> 00:56:00,253
and my tongue's all healed now.

1000
00:56:01,088 --> 00:56:04,966
I should invite you over
for a meal sometime.

1001
00:56:06,802 --> 00:56:08,011
I see.

1002
00:56:08,595 --> 00:56:10,764
Now then, you should be on your way.

1003
00:56:31,493 --> 00:56:32,494
CLOSED FOR THE DAY

1004
00:56:32,577 --> 00:56:35,330
VISITING A MAINLAND HOSPITAL
DUE TO A HAND INJURY

1005
00:56:35,414 --> 00:56:37,833
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT
STYLE
::cue()

1006
00:56:56,059 --> 00:56:57,436
Gosh.

1007
00:56:57,519 --> 00:57:00,021
Dr. Do, are you okay?

1008
00:57:00,105 --> 00:57:02,649
I'll prescribe a different medicine
for Mr. Lee.

1009
00:57:02,733 --> 00:57:03,859
[Ms. Hwang] Right.

1010
00:57:04,776 --> 00:57:07,279
Goodness me.
Mr. Park, what brings you here?

1011
00:57:12,784 --> 00:57:14,411
[Mr. Park] Have some of this.

1012
00:57:15,537 --> 00:57:17,372
Oh, my!

1013
00:57:18,039 --> 00:57:19,040
-Goodness!
-Sorry?

1014
00:57:20,500 --> 00:57:22,252
Goodness gracious!

1015
00:57:22,335 --> 00:57:23,754
Or toss it if you don't want it.

1016
00:57:23,837 --> 00:57:25,046
Dr. Do.

1017
00:57:28,175 --> 00:57:30,218
What's going on?

1018
00:57:31,136 --> 00:57:33,597
I went to the hospital to look into it.

1019
00:57:33,680 --> 00:57:36,099
Turns out the insurance company
tried to cheat him.

1020
00:57:36,183 --> 00:57:38,185
[♪ emotional music playing]

1021
00:57:38,268 --> 00:57:41,062
They rejected the claim
for Mr. Park's stent procedure

1022
00:57:41,146 --> 00:57:44,649
for myocardial infarction,
classifying it as angina instead.

1023
00:57:45,859 --> 00:57:48,028
And I just took their word for it.

1024
00:57:49,613 --> 00:57:51,782
They argued that
it wasn't myocardial infarction

1025
00:57:51,865 --> 00:57:53,992
because there was no ST segment elevation,

1026
00:57:54,075 --> 00:57:55,660
but his report clearly states

1027
00:57:55,744 --> 00:57:58,371
that it was a non-ST-segment elevation
myocardial infarction,

1028
00:57:58,455 --> 00:58:00,248
so it was indeed a myocardial infarction.

1029
00:58:00,332 --> 00:58:02,250
That means you can claim your payout.

1030
00:58:02,334 --> 00:58:03,335
Right.

1031
00:58:03,418 --> 00:58:04,544
It may take a while,

1032
00:58:04,628 --> 00:58:07,589
but you can still get your payout
if you file for compensation

1033
00:58:07,672 --> 00:58:10,550
with the Korea Consumer Agency
and make an insurance claim.

1034
00:58:10,634 --> 00:58:13,804
Wow, so you went there in person
to look into everything?

1035
00:58:14,387 --> 00:58:17,224
-Yeah.
-Goodness me, you precious thing.

1036
00:58:17,307 --> 00:58:20,560
You really were trained
at a big university hospital.

1037
00:58:20,644 --> 00:58:24,314
How are you so smart?
This is such great news.

1038
00:58:24,397 --> 00:58:25,607
I should get going now.

1039
00:58:25,690 --> 00:58:28,819
Okay, we won't walk you out.

1040
00:58:29,736 --> 00:58:31,029
And…

1041
00:58:31,112 --> 00:58:34,366
my wife will be bringing lunch
for the center tomorrow.

1042
00:58:36,117 --> 00:58:37,661
I told her to bring meat dishes.

1043
00:58:37,744 --> 00:58:38,745
Okay.

1044
00:58:39,830 --> 00:58:41,039
Dr. Do Jiui…

1045
00:58:43,750 --> 00:58:45,418
enjoy the food, okay?

1046
00:58:47,170 --> 00:58:48,797
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

1047
00:58:50,382 --> 00:58:53,134
-You precious thing.
-[Hari] I did good, didn't I?

1048
00:58:54,719 --> 00:58:55,720
Let me prepare those.

1049
00:58:55,804 --> 00:58:57,931
Sure. Just how many are there?

1050
00:58:58,014 --> 00:58:59,724
We're gonna have ourselves a feast.

1051
00:59:13,738 --> 00:59:14,781
[sighs]

1052
00:59:14,865 --> 00:59:18,368
I'LL BE OUT FOR A WHILE
I'LL LEAVE IT UP TO YOUR CONSCIENCE

1053
00:59:26,376 --> 00:59:27,961
[door opening]

1054
00:59:35,218 --> 00:59:36,761
Were you waiting for me?

1055
00:59:37,554 --> 00:59:38,638
Me, wait for you?

1056
00:59:38,722 --> 00:59:41,683
Not at all. I was just…

1057
00:59:43,101 --> 00:59:45,478
[Hari] You look like
you've got something to say.

1058
00:59:48,315 --> 00:59:49,524
If not, never mind.

1059
00:59:49,608 --> 00:59:51,026
[stammering] Thank you.

1060
00:59:52,277 --> 00:59:53,570
[scoffs]
STYLE
::cue()

1061
00:59:53,653 --> 00:59:55,655
Was that so hard?

1062
00:59:59,075 --> 01:00:00,911
Care to join me for some beer?

1063
01:00:06,333 --> 01:00:07,334
Cheers.

1064
01:00:14,049 --> 01:00:16,343
There's something I want to ask you.

1065
01:00:16,968 --> 01:00:17,969
[Jiui] Mmm.

1066
01:00:19,721 --> 01:00:21,723
Why did you send this to me?

1067
01:00:23,266 --> 01:00:25,644
I actually sent that by accident.

1068
01:00:25,727 --> 01:00:28,980
[Hari] I had a good laugh.
Isn't it hilarious?

1069
01:00:29,064 --> 01:00:30,732
Delete it.

1070
01:00:30,815 --> 01:00:33,234
[Hari] No. I'm going to look at it
whenever I feel down.

1071
01:00:41,785 --> 01:00:44,329
You should also take a look
and get a laugh out of it.

1072
01:00:46,498 --> 01:00:47,582
Okay?

1073
01:00:47,666 --> 01:00:48,667
Okay.

1074
01:00:50,543 --> 01:00:53,338
You've had a dark cloud
hanging over your head all day.

1075
01:00:57,801 --> 01:00:59,260
Did something happen?

1076
01:01:02,806 --> 01:01:04,516
Well…

1077
01:01:08,603 --> 01:01:10,897
I prescribed an NSAID to a patient

1078
01:01:12,232 --> 01:01:14,776
with a history
of myocardial infarction today.

1079
01:01:14,859 --> 01:01:15,860
What?

1080
01:01:16,361 --> 01:01:18,780
Do they know they shouldn't take it?

1081
01:01:19,614 --> 01:01:23,034
That's why I ran after him
to tell him not to take it.

1082
01:01:23,118 --> 01:01:24,536
I see.

1083
01:01:25,120 --> 01:01:27,122
Because taking it might have killed him.

1084
01:01:31,084 --> 01:01:32,293
But here's the thing…

1085
01:01:34,170 --> 01:01:37,215
I wasn't worried about the patient
as I was chasing after him.

1086
01:01:38,925 --> 01:01:40,343
I only worried about myself.

1087
01:01:42,762 --> 01:01:45,432
If someone were to find out
I prescribed the wrong meds,

1088
01:01:45,515 --> 01:01:49,019
they could have filed a complaint,
which would lead to disciplinary action

1089
01:01:49,102 --> 01:01:52,105
and me getting trapped on this island.

1090
01:01:53,773 --> 01:01:55,859
[♪ emotional music playing]

1091
01:01:55,942 --> 01:01:57,986
I ran after him to save myself.

1092
01:02:02,073 --> 01:02:03,074
But…

1093
01:02:06,703 --> 01:02:08,705
the patient thanked me.

1094
01:02:11,249 --> 01:02:12,834
For saving his life.

1095
01:02:16,921 --> 01:02:20,216
I lashed out so many times
because people looked down on PH docs…

1096
01:02:22,594 --> 01:02:24,220
but it turns out I was the one…

1097
01:02:26,890 --> 01:02:28,349
who looked down on myself most.

1098
01:02:30,143 --> 01:02:31,352
Despite being a doctor…

1099
01:02:33,438 --> 01:02:35,648
I decided to do nothing.

1100
01:02:44,699 --> 01:02:45,825
Doctor…

1101
01:02:46,951 --> 01:02:48,536
come with me.

1102
01:02:49,370 --> 01:02:50,371
What?

1103
01:02:51,331 --> 01:02:53,833
-Come on.
-What? Where…

1104
01:02:54,375 --> 01:02:55,877
You'll see when we get there.
STYLE
::cue()

1105
01:03:00,131 --> 01:03:02,175
[Jiui] What on earth are you looking for?

1106
01:03:02,258 --> 01:03:04,928
[Hari] Just give it a second.

1107
01:03:05,011 --> 01:03:07,013
There's something I want to show you.

1108
01:03:07,639 --> 01:03:09,599
[Jiui] I get that, but what is it?

1109
01:03:09,682 --> 01:03:13,228
It's not something
you can come across that easily, but…

1110
01:03:15,438 --> 01:03:16,898
That's odd.

1111
01:03:19,609 --> 01:03:22,821
They should be showing up right about now.

1112
01:03:27,408 --> 01:03:29,410
I'm going to climb my way down now.

1113
01:03:32,664 --> 01:03:34,207
[gasps] Wait!

1114
01:03:35,542 --> 01:03:36,918
Come here!

1115
01:03:37,961 --> 01:03:39,754
What is it?

1116
01:03:39,838 --> 01:03:40,922
[Hari] Be quiet.

1117
01:03:58,064 --> 01:03:59,190
[gasps]

1118
01:04:01,734 --> 01:04:02,819
[Hari giggles]

1119
01:04:02,902 --> 01:04:04,737
[♪ gentle melodic music playing]

1120
01:04:07,782 --> 01:04:09,951
[Jiui] I've never seen fireflies before.

1121
01:04:10,034 --> 01:04:11,244
[Hari] Really?

1122
01:04:11,327 --> 01:04:13,955
-[Jiui] Wow.
-[Hari laughs]

1123
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:18,209
What do you think?

1124
01:04:18,960 --> 01:04:20,170
Aren't they beautiful?

1125
01:04:23,840 --> 01:04:25,675
What did I tell you?

1126
01:04:25,758 --> 01:04:27,760
I told you they'd show up soon.

1127
01:04:31,931 --> 01:04:33,099
They're beautiful, right?

1128
01:04:46,279 --> 01:04:47,614
By the way, Dr. Do…

1129
01:04:50,992 --> 01:04:52,327
this island

1130
01:04:53,620 --> 01:04:55,830
and the people here are just as beautiful

1131
01:04:55,914 --> 01:04:58,541
when you look at them from up close.

1132
01:05:04,339 --> 01:05:08,718
I'm sorry to have to keep telling you
to bear with it all the time.

1133
01:05:10,762 --> 01:05:13,973
But you doctors are the only ones
the people here can depend on

1134
01:05:14,974 --> 01:05:16,643
when they get sick.

1135
01:05:19,354 --> 01:05:23,024
So please go easy on them. Okay?

1136
01:05:23,107 --> 01:05:24,150
[chuckles]

1137
01:05:27,320 --> 01:05:29,072
-[Jiui scoffs]
-[laughs]

1138
01:05:30,031 --> 01:05:31,199
[Jucheon grunts]

1139
01:05:35,495 --> 01:05:38,331
Dr. Chiyeon, do you want to have a beer?

1140
01:05:39,082 --> 01:05:41,501
[Hyeon] No, I'm going to sleep early.

1141
01:05:41,584 --> 01:05:43,127
I didn't get any sleep last night.

1142
01:05:43,211 --> 01:05:45,421
[♪ comical music playing]

1143
01:05:46,005 --> 01:05:49,300
[stammers] So you didn't
get any sleep on Madeokdo?

1144
01:05:49,384 --> 01:05:50,385
No.

1145
01:05:51,344 --> 01:05:52,428
Have a good rest.

1146
01:05:52,512 --> 01:05:54,973
[door opens, closes]

1147
01:05:55,473 --> 01:05:57,141
-I knew it.
-[phone pinging]

1148
01:06:00,061 --> 01:06:01,854
What's got everyone so worked up?

1149
01:06:03,564 --> 01:06:04,983
[messenger 1] Stop everything. Major PSA.

1150
01:06:05,066 --> 01:06:07,568
Has a nurse recently joined
any of your health centers?

1151
01:06:07,652 --> 01:06:10,321
Apparently, she's notorious
for being a doctor hunter!

1152
01:06:10,405 --> 01:06:11,656
[messenger 2] A doctor hunter?

1153
01:06:12,240 --> 01:06:13,658
[Jucheon] Hmm?

1154
01:06:13,741 --> 01:06:16,244
[messenger 3] Do you mean
the short-haired gold digger?

1155
01:06:16,327 --> 01:06:18,871
The one from Asong Hospital,
with the mole on her nose!

1156
01:06:18,955 --> 01:06:21,165
I heard about her from an older colleague.

1157
01:06:21,249 --> 01:06:23,584
Asong Hospital's infamous nurse
who targets doctors!
STYLE
::cue()

1158
01:06:27,130 --> 01:06:30,883
A nurse from Asong Hospital?

1159
01:06:30,967 --> 01:06:32,552
[Ms. Hwang]
Ms. Hari here is an intellectual

1160
01:06:32,635 --> 01:06:36,306
who used to work
in a university hospital's ER.

1161
01:06:36,389 --> 01:06:40,435
Not just any hospital,
but Asong Hospital… [echoing]

1162
01:06:42,520 --> 01:06:43,938
Could it be…

1163
01:06:46,607 --> 01:06:47,900
Yuk Hari?

1164
01:06:54,574 --> 01:06:56,409
Can I ask you something?

1165
01:06:57,118 --> 01:06:58,244
Mmm.

1166
01:07:01,122 --> 01:07:02,373
Why did you go to Madeokdo…

1167
01:07:04,000 --> 01:07:07,337
with Dr. Hyeon Chiyeon?

1168
01:07:08,504 --> 01:07:09,505
Oh.

1169
01:07:10,298 --> 01:07:12,675
How could I have gone there with you?

1170
01:07:12,759 --> 01:07:14,302
It's not within walking distance.

1171
01:07:16,888 --> 01:07:19,182
It's over an hour away by boat.

1172
01:07:21,726 --> 01:07:22,935
Ah.

1173
01:07:26,314 --> 01:07:28,441
So you were looking out for me.

1174
01:07:29,901 --> 01:07:31,110
I didn't even realize that.

1175
01:07:35,073 --> 01:07:37,116
But I kind of regret it.

1176
01:07:42,080 --> 01:07:43,915
Maybe I shouldn't have looked out for you…

1177
01:07:45,875 --> 01:07:48,378
and just gone there with you.

1178
01:07:59,222 --> 01:08:00,390
Next time…

1179
01:08:02,725 --> 01:08:04,352
do you want to go with me?

1180
01:08:06,646 --> 01:08:08,815
[♪ romantic music playing]

1181
01:08:32,255 --> 01:08:35,591
EVEN IF YOU THINK
YOU KNOW YOUR BODY WELL,

1182
01:08:35,675 --> 01:08:40,513
YOU NEED TO CONSULT
YOUR DOCTOR FIRST

1183
01:08:40,596 --> 01:08:45,810
THAT'S WHAT DOCTORS ARE FOR

1184
01:09:00,408 --> 01:09:04,328
YOU HAVE TO BE QUIET TO
SEE THE FIREFLIES

1185
01:09:12,420 --> 01:09:15,339
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

1186
01:09:16,174 --> 01:09:20,845
So you're saying Dr. Hyeon Chiyeon is
going out with Ms. Yuk Hari, huh?

1187
01:09:20,928 --> 01:09:23,264
[Geumja]
You could see hearts in their eyes.

1188
01:09:23,347 --> 01:09:25,850
Looks like we might be having
a wedding on Pyeondongdo!

1189
01:09:25,933 --> 01:09:27,977
It didn't seem to be just a rumor.

1190
01:09:28,060 --> 01:09:29,395
[Hyeon] Does it bother you that much?

1191
01:09:29,479 --> 01:09:30,980
[Jiui] I had no idea

1192
01:09:31,063 --> 01:09:32,565
that you and Dr. Chiyeon were…

1193
01:09:33,608 --> 01:09:35,943
So you were scared
that I'd get my hooks in?

1194
01:09:36,777 --> 01:09:38,654
[Jucheon] I'm telling you,

1195
01:09:38,738 --> 01:09:40,490
she's definitely gotten her hooks in!

1196
01:09:45,203 --> 01:09:47,205
Translated by Yoon Hyuk Park

